---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: safix/groups/oncall.nix is not a group declaration this can edit, so oncall's membership
was not touched.

This edits one `members` list as text: a line inserted or a line removed,
parsed before anything is staged. What it needs is that file, holding a
`members` list of names it can read — a list written by hand as one line or
as one name per line is both.

A declaration living somewhere else is supported, and so is a `members` value
computed rather than written: declarations merge, so where one is written is
not something safix knows. But the edit has to have a file to make, so move
the declaration to that path or edit the membership by hand.

A hand edit owes the same disclosure this verb prints: removing a subject
narrows every file the group's audience names and takes nothing back.
